      "data": {
        "text": "**Choosing TTS Provider**\n\nI'm currently focused on selecting a suitable Text-to-Speech provider for the Python script. I plan to implement the synthesis logic within `synthesize_text.py`. The goal is a Python file that effectively converts plain text into an audio byte stream using a chosen external TTS service.\n\n\n**Implementing Google TTS**\n\nI've decided to move forward with Google Cloud Text-to-Speech. I'm actively working on the `synthesize_text.py` file, incorporating the `google.cloud.texttospeech` library. The plan is coming together: I'll define a function to handle text input, leverage the Google Cloud client for synthesis, and return the resulting audio. I intend to use the `write` tool to create the file.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789862715868,
          "start": 1789862713481
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bc219889001dOkdnAV0N11PPI",
      "message_id": "msg_0bc21943d0017Mgx0pePzyKrHZ",
      "session_id": "ses_f43de6c3dffeOaYombnTIEnPOP",
      "time_created": 1789862713481,
      "time_updated": 1789862715868
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "callID": "m7CLjVl1VQIE1ASg",
        "metadata": {
          "google": {
            "thoughtSignature": ""
          }
        },
        "state": {
          "input": {
            "content": "from google.cloud import texttospeech\n\ndef synthesize_text_to_audio(text: str, voice_name: str = \"en-US-Standard-A\", audio_encoding: texttospeech.AudioEncoding = texttospeech.AudioEncoding.MP3) -> bytes:\n    \"\"\"\n    Synthesizes plain text to an audio byte stream using Google Cloud Text-to-Speech.\n\n    Args:\n        text: The plain text to synthesize.\n        voice_name: The name of the voice to use for synthesis (e.g., \"en-US-Standard-A\").\n        audio_encoding: The audio encoding for the output (e.g., MP3, LINEAR16).\n\n    Returns:\n        A bytes object containing the audio content.\n    \"\"\"\n    client = texttospeech.TextToSpeechClient()\n\n    synthesis_input = texttospeech.SynthesisInput(text=text)\n\n    # Select the type of audio file you want to generate\n    audio_config = texttospeech.AudioConfig(\n        audio_encoding=audio_encoding\n    )\n\n    # Perform the text-to-speech request\n    response = client.synthesize_speech(\n        input=synthesis_input, voice=texttospeech.VoiceSelectionParams(name=voice_name), audio_config=audio_config\n    )\n\n    return response.audio_content\n",
            "filePath": "synthesize_text.py"
          },
